# Settings of the ASP control plane (a systemd EnvironmentFile: KEY=value, one per
# line, no quotes). Mode 0600: it holds secrets. Every variable is described in
# control-plane/README.md; these are the ones a first start needs.
#
# Where to listen. The default is the loopback; nodes on other hosts need an address
# they can reach, and then TLS:
#ASP_LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8443
#ASP_TLS_CERT=/etc/asp/tls.crt
#ASP_TLS_KEY=/etc/asp/tls.key
#
# Postgres keeps sandboxes, nodes and keys across a restart; without it the store is in
# memory and a restart forgets them (stopped sandboxes keep their disks on the nodes
# until a node notices):
#ASP_DATABASE_URL=postgres://asp:CHANGE-ME@127.0.0.1:5432/asp?sslmode=disable
#
# The first API key, with the scope of every tenant, for `asp` and for nodes that have
# no client certificate yet. Pick a long random one: openssl rand -hex 24
#ASP_BOOTSTRAP_API_KEY=
#
# Shared secret a node enrolls with the first time (or issue single-use tokens with
# `asp node enroll-token`, which is better):
#ASP_NODE_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=
